{"term":"prescription","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:97dc51a32f0fe70a55","definition":"A written order from an authorized medical practitioner for provision of a medicine or other treatment, such as (ophthalmology) the specific lenses needed for a pair of glasses.","example":"The surgeon had written thousands of prescriptions for pain killers without proper examinations before the police raided the clinic.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["scrip","forescript","Rx","℞"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["coprescription","deprescription","e-prescription","misprescription","nonprescription","non-prescription","overprescription","prescription bottle","prescription drug","prescription glasses","prescriptionist","prescriptionistic","prescriptionless","represcription","underprescription"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prescription#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d06eb52771eeeee73d","definition":"The medicine or treatment provided by such an order.","example":"I need you to pick up gramma's prescriptions on your way home.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["coprescription","deprescription","e-prescription","misprescription","nonprescription","non-prescription","overprescription","prescription bottle","prescription drug","prescription glasses","prescriptionist","prescriptionistic","prescriptionless","represcription","underprescription"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prescription#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9e6b145ea9be3d052c","definition":"Any plan of treatment or handling; the treatment or handling thus provided.","example":"Early to bed and early to rise is a prescription for a long, healthy, and